WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:06.540
A stopped watch, a big red symbol, and some unique&nbsp;
monsters are just a few of the ways HBO is letting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.576
fans of "The Last of Us" know their show will&nbsp;
include plenty of familiar sights from the games.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.980
It's set in a devastated post-apocalyptic&nbsp;
world, but "The Last of Us" isn't all doom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.400
and gloom. The game does have its&nbsp;
brief and beautiful moments of hope,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.380
often shared between Joel and Ellie on their&nbsp;
long road together, with one in particular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.180
having major significance for fans. As the&nbsp;
end of the first game approaches, Joel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:35.400
Ellie come across a pair of wild giraffes who have&nbsp;
been roaming free. It's a totally new experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.380
for Ellie, beautifully captured in the game. It&nbsp;
strengthens the bond between these two strangers.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:48.278
"It's got its ups and downs. But,&nbsp;
you can't deny the view, though."

00:00:48.278 --> 00:00:52.560
There is a moment near the end of the trailer&nbsp;
for the HBO series that shows the two looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.660
at something out of shot, with Joel observing&nbsp;
Ellie's reaction rather than looking ahead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:03.240
It's entirely possible this is the live-action&nbsp;
recreation of the giraffe moment. If it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:08.303
it'll undoubtedly make viewers, die-hard&nbsp;
fans or not, sob uncontrollably.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:12.960
Besides what look to be stunning shot-for-shot&nbsp;
reenactments of major moments from the game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.460
the teaser also includes familiar and&nbsp;
unfamiliar characters. There's a brief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.540
but pretty intense first look at Nick&nbsp;
Offerman as a shotgun-toting recluse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:27.300
Bill, who appears to have his sights on Joel after&nbsp;
seemingly falling into a trap. Regardless of how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:32.640
things look, these two are on reasonably decent&nbsp;
terms, with Bill being a supply man for Joel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:37.200
Bill's just paranoid and doubtful of anyone&nbsp;
that isn't him or his loving partner, Frank.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.720
Another character, played by Melanie Lynskey,&nbsp;
also makes a brief appearance. Lynskey's name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.860
has been absent on the cast list, with&nbsp;
the actress herself even proclaiming it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:50.760
as a surprise on Twitter. Might she be&nbsp;
an all-new character in this well-known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.500
story? More importantly, just which side of&nbsp;
Joe and Ellie's journey will she end up on?

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.400
It's clear that HBO's take on&nbsp;
"The Last of Us" has tried to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.240
be as faithful to the game and its&nbsp;
characters as possible. One of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.320
trailer's first shots lingers upon&nbsp;
Joel as he sits silently. His quiet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:12.180
contemplative mood lets the camera linger on his&nbsp;
signature wristwatch. As fans of the game know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:17.160
the timepiece is a gift from Joel's late daughter,&nbsp;
Sarah. She gives it to him for his birthday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:22.380
and he wears it during their fatal escape from&nbsp;
Austin. From that point on, the watch becomes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:27.720
symbol of Joel's guilt over his survival, and how&nbsp;
his life stopped, frozen, at that very moment.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.680
Fans of the series will notice that the&nbsp;
watch on Joel's wrist is set to the exact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.423
time when it was stopped forever during&nbsp;
Joel and Sarah's desperate escape attempt.

00:02:36.423 --> 00:02:40.800
Part enraged zombie, part mushroom,&nbsp;
a Clicker is what happens when an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.000
infected person has mutated from the&nbsp;
fungal infection after ab﻿out a year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.840
Clickers use echolocation to track&nbsp;
their victims, hence their name.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.360
Shown near the tail end of the trailer,&nbsp;
these monsters are absolute nightmare fuel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:04.620
in the games. The best tactic to avoid&nbsp;
an encounter with a Clicker is to stay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:09.540
quiet and distract them if you can. But some&nbsp;
encounters are unavoidable, and we're likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.354
going to see Joel and Ellie have some very&nbsp;
intense altercations with these creatures.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:20.100
One of the first images shown in the trailer is&nbsp;
two people painting over a big red logo. Fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.880
of the video games will immediately&nbsp;
recognize this as the Firefly logo.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.900
The Fireflies are an important group&nbsp;
in both "The Last of Us" and "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.560
Last of Us Part II." They were a militia&nbsp;
group that rose up against the military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:36.180
occupation of numerous cities in the&nbsp;
United States. After the outbreak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:40.560
the United States government sent troops to&nbsp;
most of the biggest cities in the country in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.600
an attempt to restore government control, but&nbsp;
the Fireflies refused to give in. As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.340
many cities became the sites of battles&nbsp;
between the military and the Fireflies.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:55.560
In the HBO series, the Fireflies' presence&nbsp;
can be felt in the quarantine zone we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.740
Joel roaming around. Not only have&nbsp;
they already set up in the area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:04.450
but their deeds have become so infamous that&nbsp;
people need to cover up any evidence of them.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.180
At one point in the trailer, Ellie is chained&nbsp;
up, with a restraint around her ankle. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.260
normally this would be considered an abusive&nbsp;
act, "The Last of Us" fans know this is for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:17.400
a good reason. In the video game, Ellie&nbsp;
was bitten by an infected weeks earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:22.064
and we find out she's immune to the&nbsp;
usually fast-acting Cordyceps infection.

00:04:22.205 --> 00:04:23.105
"Look at this!"

00:04:23.427 --> 00:04:25.226
"I don't care how you got infected."

00:04:25.936 --> 00:04:27.497
"It's three weeks old."

00:04:27.652 --> 00:04:32.160
This suggests she could provide a cure that&nbsp;
the crumbling world is desperate for. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.360
smugglers are better safe than sorry when&nbsp;
it comes to risking a brain-eating virus.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:41.280
Obviously, Ellie doesn't stay restrained for&nbsp;
long. And her immunity to the virus is why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.660
she needs to get across the country, but&nbsp;
things somehow only get worse for Ellie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.819
Joel, and Tess as they make&nbsp;
their way to the Fireflies.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.680
While Joel's friends might be scattered&nbsp;
throughout the post-apocalyptic world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.580
one person that stands beside him,&nbsp;
for a while at least, is his brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.580 --> 00:05:01.680
Tommy. Seen for a split second, looking through&nbsp;
a fire at his brother, this take on the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.960
is played by Gabriel Luna, who has appeared&nbsp;
in as many big franchises as Pedro Pascal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.100
who plays Joel. The former Ghost Rider&nbsp;
from "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D" and one-time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:16.080
Terminator is fighting for his life just&nbsp;
like everyone else in HBO's upcoming show;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.640
it's just a question of how that will impact&nbsp;
his relationship with his on-screen big brother.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:25.500
In the game, Tommy is seen at the start of the&nbsp;
virus before dipping off the radar and forcing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.060
Joel to reunite with him. Their meet-up&nbsp;
is a tense one for complicated reasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:33.120
so it'll be interesting to see&nbsp;
just how much he'll be present&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.115
in the series and how long it'll be&nbsp;
before he and Joel team up again.

